Package: mdeinR
Type: Package
Title: Memorable Dining Experience (MDE) Text Analysis
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Gopi Nath", "Vajpai", email = "gvajpai@udel.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Timothy", "Webb", email = "twebb@udel.edu", role = "aut"),
    person("Srikanth", "Beldona", email = "beldona@udel.edu", role = "aut"),
    person("Tyler W.", "Rinker", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Scoring algorithm and valence-shifter design derived from sentimentr <https://github.com/trinker/sentimentr>")
  )
Description: Provides tools to detect and score the five dimensions of
    Memorable Dining Experiences (MDE) — sensory, affective, behavioral,
    social, and intellectual — from free-text restaurant reviews using a
    theoretically grounded lexicon. Implements sentence-level scoring with
    valence-shifter (negator/amplifier/de-amplifier/adversative) adjustment,
    a built-in sentence tokeniser, and a bundled valence-shifter table —
    all without external NLP dependencies. Based on the lexicon described
    in Vajpai, Webb & Beldona (2025) <doi:10.1016/j.ijhm.2025.104245>.
